      "statusChangeID": "67adbb3ac858d4164c73ba0b",
      "statusChangeNewStatus": "closed",
      "value": "We aren't planning to change the formatting of our log files at this time. Condensing these files makes it easier to debug issues with them, which is their main purpose. We'd rather not risk modifying written messages, since we're aware of some worlds that read the log file back again that may depend on exact characters making their way into the log file as written.\n\nRegarding your use case, if you're monitoring the file while VRChat is actively writing to it, I feel you should be able to read to the end of the file to find the most recent log statement? VRChat will only write whole log statements each time it updates the file.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
